  "description": "High and low tide tables for Australian beaches, up to 7 days ahead, for surfers, fishers and beachgoers.",
  "readme": "# TideBot\n\n## Summary\n\nTideBot gives tide times and heights for beaches across Australia, with daily high and low tides for up to 7 days ahead. Ask it about any named beach and it returns a simple tide table you can read at a glance. It is built for surfers, fishers, swimmers and anyone planning a day by the sea.\n\n## Key features\n\n- Daily tide tables showing high and low tides with times and heights\n- Covers Australian beaches, from city classics to quiet coastal spots\n- Look ahead up to 7 days, so weekend plans can be made early\n- Plain-language answers instead of raw data dumps\n\n## Usage\n\nSend a message naming a beach and, optionally, a day. TideBot replies with a tide table for that spot and date.\n\n    User: tides for Bondi tomorrow\n    TideBot: Tide table for Bondi Beach, NSW, tomorrow: Low 1:12 am (0.35 m), High 7:40 am (1.62 m), Low 1:55 pm (0.28 m), High 8:05 pm (1.71 m). Times are local.\n\n## Use cases\n\nSurfers can pick the best session window, fishers can plan around tide changes, and swimmers or families can time a safer swim or avoid exposed flats. It also helps with boat ramp trips, rock fishing, beach photography at low tide, and everyday coastal planning anywhere in Australia.\n\n## Limitations\n\nTideBot covers Australian beaches only and needs a beach or place name it recognises; vague requests may need a quick follow-up. Heights are predictions, not observations, and accuracy lessens the further ahead you ask. It does not cover overseas locations or real-time safety warnings, and it should not replace official maritime notices.\n\n## Metadata\n\nVersion: 1.0.0. Category: Weather and marine. Source of data: astronomical tidal predictions for Australian reference stations, adjusted to nearby beaches.\n",
  "keywords": [
    "tide times",
    "tide tables",
    "Australian beaches",
    "high and low tides",
    "up to 7 days ahead"
  ],
  "starter_prompts": [
    "What are the tides for Bondi Beach tomorrow?",
    "Can you give me the tide table for Byron Bay this weekend?",
    "When is the next high tide at Manly?"
  ]
}"}}

