{"description": "Extracts supplier, total amount and due date from pasted invoice text for small teams.", "readme": "# Invoice Helper\n\n## Summary\nInvoice Helper reads invoice text you paste and returns the supplier, total amount and due date in a short table, so small teams can log bills fast. It is built for small teams that need the key details from pasted invoice text without reading every line themselves. No setup is needed: paste the invoice text and ask for what you want.\n\n## Key features\n- Extracts the supplier name from pasted invoice text\n- Returns the total amount on each invoice\n- Finds the invoice due date so bills are paid on time\n- Shows supplier, total, due date and currency in one short table\n- Handles AUD, USD and EUR amounts\n\n## Usage\nPaste the invoice text into the chat and ask for the supplier, total or due date.\n\n    User: Here is the invoice text from our supplier. What is the total amount?\n    Agent: Supplier Acme Supplies, total amount 1,240.00 EUR, due date 30 June 2025.\n\n## Use cases\nSmall teams that receive invoices by email can paste the text here to log bills fast without reading each one line by line. Office admins and bookkeepers can pull the total amount and due date straight into their payment tracker. Freelancers can check when each supplier invoice is due before paying it.\n\n## Limitations\nText only; no scanned images or PDF attachments, so copy the invoice as text before pasting. Handles AUD, USD and EUR; other currencies may be misread. Extraction depends on the pasted text being complete and readable, so results may be wrong if the invoice text is unclear or truncated.\n\n## Metadata\n- Version: 1.0.0\n- Category: Finance and invoicing\n- Data source: the invoice text pasted by the user; no external data sources are used", "keywords": ["invoice text", "supplier name", "total amount", "invoice due date", "small teams"], "starter_prompts": ["What is the total amount on this invoice?", "Who is the supplier on this invoice?", "When is this invoice due?", "Can you extract the supplier, total and due date from this invoice text?"]}
